  "name": "Example: Identifying the Formula For Negating a Quantified Statement",
  "problem": "What is the negation of the following statement?\n\n$$\n\\forall y \\in \\overline{S}, \\, \\neg P(y)\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "To negate the universal statement $\\forall y \\in \\overline{S}, \\, \\neg P(y),$ we flip the quantifier to existential and negate the predicate: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00ac(\u2200y\\in \\overset{\u2015}{S},\\,\u00acP(y)) & \u2261\u2203y\\in \\overset{\u2015}{S},\\,\u00ac\u00acP(y) \\\\  & \u2261\u2203y\\in \\overset{\u2015}{S},\\,P(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
